data:{"id":"11317268-e5dd-485a-b329-ca623a01faf0","response_type":"tool_result","content":"","done":false,"data":{"duration_ms":9,"error":"","found_kbs":{"concept/command-line-interface":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"],"concept/multi-tasking-operating-system":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"],"concept/network-operating-system":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"],"concept/open-source-operating-system":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581","fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"],"concept/unix-like-operating-system":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"],"entity/chrome-os":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581","fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"],"entity/dos":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"],"entity/freebsd":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581","fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"],"entity/linux":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581","fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"],"entity/linux-mint":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581","fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"],"entity/ubuntu":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"],"entity/unix":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581","fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"],"summary/d4fdffd0-5c7d-4290-adbb-f5e1f7ae80b0":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"],"summary/ee9f60e3-062c-49cb-bad4-d8ccd3e8083c":["fed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581"]},"output":"\u003csearch_results count=\"10\" query=\"操作系统|operating system\"\u003e\n\u003cpage\u003e\n\u003cknowledge_base_id\u003efed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581\u003c/knowledge_base_id\u003e\n\u003clink\u003e[[concept/multi-tasking-operating-system|Multi-tasking Operating System]]\u003c/link\u003e\n\u003ctype\u003econcept\u003c/type\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eA multi-tasking operating system enables the concurrent execution of multiple processes or tasks, a capability found in systems like UNIX and Linux.\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003cmatch_snippet\u003e... # Multi-tasking Operating System **Multi-tasking Operating System**: An operating system ca ...\u003c/match_snippet\u003e\n\u003c/page\u003e\n\u003cpage\u003e\n\u003cknowledge_base_id\u003efed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581\u003c/knowledge_base_id\u003e\n\u003clink\u003e[[concept/network-operating-system|Network Operating System]]\u003c/link\u003e\n\u003ctype\u003econcept\u003c/type\u003e\n\u003caliases\u003eNOS\u003c/aliases\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eA Network Operating System supports workstations, personal computers, and terminals on a local area network. UNIX is cited as an example that functions as both an independent and network operating system.\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003cmatch_snippet\u003e... # Network Operating System A Network Operating System is an operating system designed ...\u003c/match_snippet\u003e\n\u003c/page\u003e\n\u003cpage\u003e\n\u003cknowledge_base_id\u003efed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581\u003c/knowledge_base_id\u003e\n\u003clink\u003e[[concept/unix-like-operating-system|Unix-like operating system]]\u003c/link\u003e\n\u003ctype\u003econcept\u003c/type\u003e\n\u003caliases\u003e类 Unix 操作系统\u003c/aliases\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eA Unix-like operating system is a category of systems behaving similarly to Unix, including Linux and FreeBSD, which share similar software ecosystems despite kernel differences.\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003cmatch_snippet\u003e... # Unix-like operating system A Unix-like operating system is a category of operating sy ...\u003c/match_snippet\u003e\n\u003c/page\u003e\n\u003cpage\u003e\n\u003cknowledge_base_id\u003efed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581\u003c/knowledge_base_id\u003e\n\u003clink\u003e[[concept/open-source-operating-system|Open-source operating system]]\u003c/link\u003e\n\u003ctype\u003econcept\u003c/type\u003e\n\u003caliases\u003e开源操作系统\u003c/aliases\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eThis page defines open-source operating systems as platforms with publicly accessible source code, highlighting Linux distributions like Ubuntu and Mint, as well as FreeBSD.\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003cmatch_snippet\u003e... # Open-source operating system Open-source operating systems are software platforms whose ...\u003c/match_snippet\u003e\n\u003c/page\u003e\n\u003cpage\u003e\n\u003cknowledge_base_id\u003efed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581\u003c/knowledge_base_id\u003e\n\u003clink\u003e[[entity/linux|Linux]]\u003c/link\u003e\n\u003ctype\u003eentity\u003c/type\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eLinux is a popular, free, multi-tasking Unix-like operating system recommended for PC users seeking alternatives to Windows, with Ubuntu and Linux Mint being notable distributions.\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003cmatch_snippet\u003e... is a popular, free, multi-tasking [[entity/unix|UNIX]]-like operating system widely used in computing environments. It is classified as ...\u003c/match_snippet\u003e\n\u003c/page\u003e\n\u003cpage\u003e\n\u003cknowledge_base_id\u003efed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581\u003c/knowledge_base_id\u003e\n\u003clink\u003e[[entity/unix|UNIX]]\u003c/link\u003e\n\u003ctype\u003eentity\u003c/type\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eUNIX is a multi-tasking, command-line operating system that functions as both an independent and network OS across various hardware architectures.\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003cmatch_snippet\u003e... # UNIX UNIX is a robust operating system designed to function across a wide variety of computer hard ...\u003c/match_snippet\u003e\n\u003c/page\u003e\n\u003cpage\u003e\n\u003cknowledge_base_id\u003efed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581\u003c/knowledge_base_id\u003e\n\u003clink\u003e[[entity/dos|DOS]]\u003c/link\u003e\n\u003ctype\u003eentity\u003c/type\u003e\n\u003caliases\u003e磁盘操作系统, Disk Operating System\u003c/aliases\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDOS is an early personal computer operating system that uses a text-based command-line interface, requiring users to type commands at a prompt like c:\\\u003e to manage files and run applications.\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003cmatch_snippet\u003e... # DOS DOS (Disk Operating System, 磁盘操作系统) is one of the first major operating systems for pe ...\u003c/match_snippet\u003e\n\u003c/page\u003e\n\u003cpage\u003e\n\u003cknowledge_base_id\u003efed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581\u003c/knowledge_base_id\u003e\n\u003clink\u003e[[entity/freebsd|FreeBSD]]\u003c/link\u003e\n\u003ctype\u003eentity\u003c/type\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eFreeBSD is an open-source operating system that uses a different kernel than Linux but shares much of the same software ecosystem, offering a similar desktop experience.\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003cmatch_snippet\u003e... # FreeBSD FreeBSD is an open-source operating system. Although it utilizes a different kernel compared to [[enti ...\u003c/match_snippet\u003e\n\u003c/page\u003e\n\u003cpage\u003e\n\u003cknowledge_base_id\u003efed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581\u003c/knowledge_base_id\u003e\n\u003clink\u003e[[entity/chrome-os|Chrome OS]]\u003c/link\u003e\n\u003ctype\u003eentity\u003c/type\u003e\n\u003caliases\u003e铬操作系统\u003c/aliases\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eChrome OS is an operating system mentioned as an alternative to Windows for personal computers, listed alongside Linux and FreeBSD in discussions of non-Windows computing platforms.\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003cmatch_snippet\u003e... # Chrome OS Chrome OS (referred to as \"铬操作系统\" in some sources) is an operating system mentioned in the c ...\u003c/match_snippet\u003e\n\u003c/page\u003e\n\u003cpage\u003e\n\u003cknowledge_base_id\u003efed4ec72-0043-49ac-b350-19a4c5a3a581\u003c/knowledge_base_id\u003e\n\u003clink\u003e[[entity/linux-mint|Linux Mint]]\u003c/link\u003e\n\u003ctype\u003eentity\u003c/type\u003e\n\u003caliases\u003eMint\u003c/aliases\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eLinux Mint is a popular Linux distribution recommended for personal computers as a user-friendly, stable, and secure alternative to proprietary operating systems.\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003cmatch_snippet\u003e... These systems provide a robust alternative to proprietary operating systems, offering stability, security, and a wide range of softwar